{
  "abstract": "For r ≥ 4 and 1 ≤ j ≤ r − 3, a finite r-uniform hypergraph with at least one edge has zero uniform Turán density at level j exactly when its vertices admit an ordering in which each shared (j + 1)-set occupies the same positions in the edges containing it. For any family of such forbidden graphs, a positive uniform Turán density is at least N⁻ᴺ, where N is the binomial coefficient r choose (j + 1). This covers infinite forbidden families as well as finite ones. The development formalizes Theorem 1.1 of Heng Li and Xizhi Liu.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Xizhi Liu"
    }
  ],
